lements of <MATH_0003>. (This is not strictly necessary,\nand in fact the example works perfectly well even if all <MATH_0004>\nare equal to <MATH_0005>.)\nConsider the graded <MATH_0006>-algebra\n<MATH_0007>\nwith grading given by <MATH_0008> and <MATH_0009>.\nThen <MATH_0010> has ample invertible sheaf\n<MATH_0011>. We claim that if <MATH_0012>\nis very ample, then <MATH_0013>. The reason for this is that <MATH_0014>\nhas degree <MATH_0015>, and hence <MATH_0016> for <MATH_0017>. Details omitted.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fcec871837b7edc36af0432e9b1b85f615e9f5aa8327f39c99d20c0ca350f73f", "unit_id": "inventory:morphisms:01VP:example/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:d457f5c24e5178dc6c8d87448a4a3c929f262ee5d2133715fa77b616bd980b24", "hash": "sha256:d457f5c24e5178dc6c8d87448a4a3c929f262ee5d2133715fa77b616bd980b24", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 331576, "byte_start": 331164, "file": "morphisms.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:518e657551bc6b448a3535a1e58a4a88e687d7ece94417a693aa2c8d736bf93b", "line_end": 9143, "line_start": 9135}, "owner_tag": "01VQ", "parent_tag": "01VL", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01VL", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-section-separation-axioms}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-immersions-monomorphisms}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{constructions-lemma-proj-separated}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2cdd54c91172842da7935e351b2e537dfc65808da525fec53dd82898c278104", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:52637f248c2181218435c9c8fd21b9e303a5ee33ce28dc3558ca988d71baafa0", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nBeing separated is local on the base (see\nSchemes, Section <REF_0001>).\nAn immersion is separated\n(see Schemes, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nHence the lemma follows since locally <MATH_0001> has an immersion into\nthe homogeneous spectrum of a graded ring which is separated, see\nConstructions, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:49c5276cc0f47944127ea238934e1907670b97d6db0eee02ae40654d66caad36", "unit_id": "inventory:morphisms:01VQ:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:30c2cec85e7010df3767a64eb524120ad4bb2476065470d09f49c8faccf7102d", "hash": "sha256:30c2cec85e7010df3767a64eb524120ad4bb2476065470d09f49c8faccf7102d", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 331162, "byte_start": 330924, "file": "morphisms.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:6ee2f7f8e2c2a50ff9df6a91a117599456debefc95fe0590368074fbbafd91e6", "line_end": 9133, "line_start": 9127}, "owner_tag": "01VQ", "parent_tag": "01VL", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01VL", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-relatively-very-ample-separated}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{L}$", "MATH_0005": "$X/S$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fb969b1e81a342aabb975a01ab2e11c33de79117b5e2faacfcde0a882e912780", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:22ee32228f2133ebca11604d735992e1e99e8d17975c5459f1ac430bd4eb7960", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an invertible sheaf on <MATH_0003>.\nIf <MATH_0004> is relatively very ample on <MATH_0005> then\n<MATH_0006> is separated.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a1d560