252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:de407da0feb1d7a32e38d602cdd46b0a8b04758809b00cb6e63d745de7b3f6e5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a2b7849c7cb515b055158f452d4782445cd3718ed4d82dc13c65500ed0c56cd5", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an invertible sheaf on <MATH_0003>.\nAssume <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact. The following are\nequivalent\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0005> is relatively very ample on <MATH_0006>,\n<STRUCT_0004> there exists an open covering <MATH_0007> such\nthat <MATH_0008> is relatively very ample\non <MATH_0009> for all <MATH_0010>,\n<STRUCT_0005> there exists a quasi-coherent sheaf of graded\n<MATH_0011>-algebras <MATH_0012> generated in degree\n<MATH_0013> over <MATH_0014> and a map of graded <MATH_0015>-algebras\n<MATH_0016>\nsuch that <MATH_0017> is surjective and the\nassociated morphism\n<MATH_0018>\nis an immersion, and\n<STRUCT_0006> <MATH_0019> is quasi-separated, the canonical map\n<MATH_0020> is surjective, and\nthe associated map <MATH_0021>\nis an immersion.\n<STRUCT_0007>\n<STRUCT_0008>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b2e74a028a5493c033008793195b72c53bb77d652a27dbbb89e74da42ff02801", "unit_id": "inventory:morphisms:01VR:lemma/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:5377817726cb7b9fd8600e26cb1abcae9957215d5024306167911e3ccf85cdd8", "hash": "sha256:5377817726cb7b9fd8600e26cb1abcae9957215d5024306167911e3ccf85cdd8", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 46572, "byte_start": 46450, "file": "constructions.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:7c071c68e305022a8c51295ab5cac77fa7ff6a577122b65ea2bf376f6b8ecd11", "line_end": 1318, "line_start": 1314}, "owner_tag": "01MC", "parent_tag": "01M3", "requested_label": "constructions-lemma-proj-separated", "requested_tag": "01MC", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "constructions", "node_kind": "lemma", "